# IMP-01 (D-1; REQ-005, AC-005) the node serves user files by byte range with a strong ETag and no-cache: base, then the fix
# command: cd autobyteus-server-ts && pnpm exec vitest run tests/unit/api/rest/user-file-ranges.test.ts   (base code, then the fix)
#          pnpm exec vitest run tests/unit/api tests/unit/node-files tests/architecture/user-file-replies.test.ts tests/unit/node-access
#          env -i PATH="$PATH" HOME=<resolved temp> TMPDIR="$TMPDIR" pnpm exec vitest run tests/e2e/node-files/node-files.e2e.test.ts
#            tests/integration/api/rest/context-files.integration.test.ts tests/integration/api/rest/workspace-content-after-restart.integration.test.ts
#            tests/e2e/remote-access/request-origin-and-phone-routes.e2e.test.ts
# commit: base 4b73fccae2 (red); 66534ef01c (fix)
# env: macOS arm64, Node v22.23.1
# date: 2026-11-24
# result: Reproduced, then fixed. On the base every one of the 18 range cases fails (whole file, no Accept-Ranges, no ETag,
#   no 206/416/304). With D-1 all pass: one range (a-b, a-, -n) 206 with exactly its bytes and Content-Range; 416 with
#   "bytes */size" for an unsatisfiable range; a multi-range or malformed Range answers the whole file (200);
#   If-None-Match with the current version 304 (a list, W/, *); If-Range serves the range only for the current version;
#   Cache-Control: no-cache, and a route's own no-store is kept; no Last-Modified; a rewritten file answers its new bytes
#   and a new ETag, never 304 for the old one; HEAD answers the headers. Per route: workspace content and static (F1, F2),
#   uploaded media (F3), run/Team/Org file changes (F9-F11, no-store kept), context files, node files (a paired phone over
#   the real node access gate, 401 without the credential); message references stay whole (no file path, FU-001).

